      "writtenOn": "2020-07-08T19:00:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at our own use case as well as people running into the same issue [1][2], it seems like users usually don\u0027t care about decoding unknown PKCS12Attributes. encoding might be a different story and it looks like openssl goes to some trouble to ensure that this can happen when creating a PKCS12 cert.\n\nNow I am inclined to simply drop this error. If that is okay, let me know and I can make the changes.\n\n[1]: https://github.com/golang/go/issues/24325\n[2]: https://github.com/SSLMate/go-pkcs12/pull/4",
      "parentUuid": "b8b51e2b_d49863ed",
